==Scottish League Cup==
{{Main|2018–19 Scottish League Cup}}
On 29 July, Celtic were drawn to face [[Partick Thistle F.C.|Partick Thistle]] at [[Firhill Stadium]] in the second round of the [[2018–19 Scottish League Cup]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14670 | title=Celtic face Partick Thistle in League Cup last 16 | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=29 July 2018 | access-date=19 August 2018 | archive-date=20 August 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180820074642/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14670 | url-status=live }}</ref> The League Cup holders progressed to the quarter-finals with a 3–1 victory over their city rivals. On 19 August, Celtic were drawn to face [[St Johnstone F.C.|St Johnstone]] at [[McDiarmid Park]] in the quarter-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14797 | title=Celtic face St Johnstone in League Cup quarter-final | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=19 August 2018 | access-date=19 August 2018 | archive-date=20 August 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180820074538/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14797 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Bhoys' trophy defence continued courtesy of a late [[Leigh Griffiths]] strike in [[Perth, Scotland|Perth]]. On 26 September, Celtic were drawn to face [[Heart of Midlothian F.C.|Heart of Midlothian]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/15014 | title=Celtic will face Hearts in League Cup semi-final | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=26 September 2018 | access-date=26 September 2018 | archive-date=27 September 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180927005557/http://www.celticfc.net/news/15014 | url-status=live }}</ref> Goals from [[Scott Sinclair]], [[James Forrest (footballer, born 1991)|James Forrest]] and [[Ryan Christie]] secured Celtic's place in the final, a third consecutive League Cup final and fifth consecutive domestic cup final in [[Brendan Rodgers]]' reign. On 2 December, Celtic won the [[Scottish League Cup]] for the third consecutive season, defeating [[Aberdeen F.C.|Aberdeen]] [[2018–19 Scottish League Cup#Final|1–0]] in the [[2018 Scottish League Cup Final|final]].

