==UEFA Champions League==
{{Main|2018–19 UEFA Champions League}}
Celtic entered the Champions League at the first qualifying round.

===First qualifying round===
On 19 June, Celtic were drawn to face [[FC Alashkert|Alashkert]] ([[Armenia]]) in the first qualifying round of the [[2018–19 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14520 | title=Celtic face Alashkert of Armenia in Champions League qualifier | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=19 June 2018 | access-date=19 June 2018 | archive-date=19 June 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180619140457/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14520 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Bhoys won 3–0 in both legs – courtesy of goals from [[Odsonne Édouard]], [[James Forrest (footballer, born 1991)|James Forrest]], [[Callum McGregor]] and [[Moussa Dembélé (French footballer)|Moussa Dembélé]] – and secured a place in the next round.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14584 | title=Edouard on target as Celts cruise to victory in Armenia | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=10 July 2018 | access-date=19 July 2018 | archive-date=19 July 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180719173805/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14584 | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14624 | title=Dembele at the double as Celts ease past Alashkert | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=18 July 2018 | access-date=19 July 2018 | archive-date=19 July 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180719173950/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14624 | url-status=live }}</ref>

