===Second qualifying round===
On 18 July, it was determined that Celtic would face [[Rosenborg BK|Rosenborg]] (Norway) in the second qualifying round of the [[2018–19 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14625 | title=Manager proud of his players as Celtic march on in Europe | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=18 July 2018 | access-date=19 July 2018 | archive-date=19 July 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180719174111/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14625 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Scottish champions eliminated the Norwegian side in the [[2017–18 UEFA Champions League#Third qualifying round|previous season's qualifying phase]] and did so again. Goals from [[Odsonne Édouard]] and [[Olivier Ntcham]] secured Celtic's passage into the next round.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14650 | title=Magnifique fightback puts Celts in pole position against Rosenborg | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=25 July 2018 | access-date=17 August 2018 | archive-date=17 August 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180817225647/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14650 | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14693 | title=Resolute Celts hold firm to march on in Europe | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=1 August 2018 | access-date=17 August 2018 | archive-date=17 August 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180817225532/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14693 | url-status=live }}</ref>

