==UEFA Europa League==
{{Main|2018–19 UEFA Europa League}}

===Play-Off round===
On 16 August, it was determined that Celtic would face [[FK Sūduva Marijampolė|Sūduva]] ([[Lithuania]]) in the Play-Off Round of the [[2018–19 UEFA Europa League|UEFA Europa League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14784 | title=Celtic v FK Suduva Europa League play-off tickets on sale now | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=17 August 2018 | access-date=17 August 2018 | archive-date=17 August 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180817131639/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14784 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Bhoys last faced the Lithuanian side in the [[2002–03 UEFA Cup first round]]; a 10–1 aggregate victory marked the beginning of Celtic's path to the [[2003 UEFA Cup Final|final]] in [[Seville]].

