*'''Home:''' The home kit features a bespoke tonal tartan design throughout the traditional green and white hoops. White shorts and hooped socks complete the look.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14268 | title=New Balance Reveals Celtic 2018/19 Home Kit | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=23 April 2018 | access-date=28 April 2018 | archive-date=28 April 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180428181407/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14268 | url-status=live }}</ref>
*'''Away:''' The away kit also features a tartan design set against White and Eden Green. The shirt is accompanied by Eden Green shorts and hooped socks.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14519 | title=Celtic's new 2018/19 New Balance away kit is officially revealed | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=19 June 2018 | access-date=2 July 2018 | archive-date=2 July 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180702204928/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14519 | url-status=live }}</ref>
*'''Third:''' The third kit features a bold black and yellow design and is inspired by the club's famous bumble-bee kits of the past. Black shorts and hooped socks complete the look.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/14629 | title=New Balance Reveals Celtic 2018/19 Third Kit | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=20 July 2018 | access-date=1 August 2018 | archive-date=2 August 2018 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180802011250/http://www.celticfc.net/news/14629 | url-status=live }}</ref>

